title: Log commands in the GUI
tags: [[Event log]]
kind: guide
summary: Undo, redo, revert, label and prune from the GUI — confirmations before, files carried along, no questions while the repository is locked.

* <<key "log:undo" Ctrl+z>> / <<key "log:redo" Ctrl+Shift+z>> — from anywhere: the same selection as `mf log undo`/`redo` ([[Undo and redo]]). A change written in one label is undone at once; one written in several (a command inside a script's answer and run) asks which, in the command input's completion, innermost first. `log:undo <label>` names it. Nothing else is asked — the result is itself undoable.
* <<key "log:revert" "p z">> — reverts what the log panel has selected: the label, or the single operation under the cursor ("undo just this one field" in one key). A confirmation names how many operations it undoes, says when files will move and how many of them overwrite a later change ([[Reverting onto the current state]]), and warns when the target was already undone. `log:revert op` narrows from a label row (asking which operation when there are several), <<key "log:revert label" "p Shift+z">> widens back.
* `log:prune` — after a confirmation, prunes everything before the selected label, for good ([[Pruning the log]]).

''Files are carried with the metadata.'' Every revert the GUI writes — undo and redo
included — goes through the same code as the CLI (`core::navigation`): one atomic request
when no operation touches a file, otherwise the coordinated form — moving a file back, bringing content back
from the trash, sending it back there ([[Filesystem coordination]]). Every confirmation
comes ''before'' the repository is locked, and nothing asks while it is: a move is applied
whether or not the file is where the log says (when it is not, the metadata keeps the
recorded path). What the file actions had to report follows the summary in the status bar.
The panels refresh afterwards.
